  "pages": [
    {
      "name": "intro",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "html",
          "name": "intro_overview",
          "html": "<h3>Purpose</h3><p>This survey measures what people believe Wyoming should do about grizzly bear delisting, management, safety, livestock loss, hunting, habitat, and long-term recovery. The goal is clarity, not persuasion.</p><h3>Plain-language definitions</h3><ul><li><strong>Delisting:</strong> For this survey, delisting means removing Greater Yellowstone grizzly bears from federal Endangered Species Act protection and returning primary management authority to the states.</li><li><strong>Connectivity:</strong> Natural movement or exchange between grizzly populations, which can affect long-term genetic health.</li><li><strong>Conflict-based removal:</strong> Removing individual bears after repeated livestock or public-safety conflicts.</li></ul><h3>How responses will be used</h3><ul><li>Results will be published in aggregate.</li><li>Exact wording and response options will be published with results.</li><li>A revision log will show what changed and why.</li><li>Individual responses remain private.</li></ul><h3>Before you begin</h3><p>This is not a test of expertise. If you are still forming a view, answer as best you can and use Not sure where it fits.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "baseline_view",
      "title": "Section 1: Baseline view",
      "description": "Start with your current familiarity, overall position, and main concern.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "issue_familiarity",
          "title": "How familiar are you with the issue of grizzly bear delisting in Wyoming?",
          "choices": [
